WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.240
COVID-19 was disastrous for Latin America.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.740
Not only because of a death
rate eight times higher

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.410
than in the world at large,

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.020
the pandemic has also
created the preconditions

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.740
for a resurgence of left wing populism,

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:13.840
that poses a threat

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.310
to personal freedom and economic wellbeing

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:17.490
throughout the region.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.430
Following months of violent
protests in Colombia,

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:23.510
Gustavo Petro became the
leading presidential candidate,

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:26.590
with proposals to raise
taxes, seize private land,

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:30.180
expand entitlements, and kneecap
the oil and gas industries.

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.010
In Peru, the socialist
president, Pedro Castillo,

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.710
was elected with the promise
of weakening property rights,

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:37.710
and rewriting the constitution

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.810
to allow for a dramatic
expansion of state power.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.560
In Argentina, President Alberto Fernandez

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.180
has responded to rapid inflation,
and a shrinking economy,

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.470
by imposing price controls, raising taxes,

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.350
and growing the regulatory state.

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.620
And in Chile, although
poverty has plummeted

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.920
in the last 20 years,

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.550
voters opted to redraft the constitution,

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:00.120
which could enshrine into law
more government intervention

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:03.370
in the economy, while weakening
private property rights.

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.120
Argentinian born libertarian,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.910
the Atlas Network's associate director

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.550
at the center for Latin America,

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.208
and the author of four
books about the region.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.100
In 2018, Marty had a televised debate

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.610
with Juan Carlos Junio,

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.200
a prominent communist
political leader in Argentina,

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.710
who exemplifies this problem

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:25.960
of exalting political figures as saviors.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.320
This attitude was on display

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:33.562
at a 2016 celebration for the
Cuban dictator, Fidel Castro.

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.370
The Castro Regime impoverished the nation,

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:00.690
drove over 1.4 million to flee,

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:02.998
and murdered thousands of dissidents.

00:04:13.368 --> 00:04:15.830
In 2018, Marty debated Patricio del Corro,

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:19.047
a socialist and congressional
representative for the city of

00:04:19.047 --> 00:04:20.038
Buenos Aires.

00:04:45.805 --> 00:04:48.471
"This misconception that the
rich are rich because the poor

00:04:48.471 --> 00:04:50.189
are poor" Marty says,

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:52.138
"traces back to the 'Open
Veins of Latin America.'"

00:04:52.138 --> 00:04:54.658
Five centuries of the
pillage of a continent,

00:04:54.658 --> 00:04:59.088
published in 1971 by the
Uruguayan writer, Eduardo Galeano.

00:04:59.088 --> 00:05:01.510
It sold over a million copies,

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:04.330
and the Venezuelan socialist
leader, Hugo Chavez,

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:08.027
famously gifted it to president
Obama at a 2009 summit.

00:05:08.027 --> 00:05:09.830
"The winners happened to have one thanks

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:11.437
to our losing" Galeano wrote.

00:05:11.437 --> 00:05:14.530
"Our defeat was always implicit
in the victory of others;

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.960
our wealth has always
generated our poverty

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.235
by nourishing the prosperity of others."

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:15.470
In 2019,

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.910
Marty debated the Colombian
political scientist

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:20.890
and aspiring politicians Sergio Fernandez,

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.240
who believes that the United States

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.030
is the world's wealthiest country

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:26.180
because of its protectionist policies,

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:28.454
and that Latin America
should follow its example.

